Give the keyboard to the next window when the focused one unmaps

cage moves the keyboard to the window underneath only when the focused window is destroyed.
Couch's launcher steps behind YouTube by unmapping its window (launcher/src/stacking.rs), so
without this nobody had the keyboard and the remote did nothing in YouTube.

For Couch (https://github.com/alecschoen/couch), on top of Raspberry Pi OS's cage 0.3.1,
after couch-background.patch.

--- a/xdg_shell.c
+++ b/xdg_shell.c
@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@
 #include <wlr/types/wlr_xdg_shell.h>
 #include <wlr/util/log.h>
 
+#include "seat.h"
 #include "server.h"
 #include "view.h"
 #include "xdg_shell.h"
@@ -222,8 +223,18 @@
 {
 	struct cg_xdg_shell_view *xdg_shell_view = wl_container_of(listener, xdg_shell_view, unmap);
 	struct cg_view *view = &xdg_shell_view->view;
+	struct cg_server *server = view->server;
+	bool focused = seat_get_focus(server->seat) == view;
 
 	view_unmap(view);
+
+	/* Couch: cage gives the keyboard to the next view only when the focused one is
+	   destroyed. Do the same when it unmaps, so a window that hides itself (Couch's
+	   launcher stepping behind YouTube) hands the keyboard to the window under it. */
+	if (focused && !wl_list_empty(&server->views)) {
+		struct cg_view *next = wl_container_of(server->views.next, next, link);
+		seat_set_focus(server->seat, next);
+	}
 }
 
 static void
